    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24302" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inter-lābor</span></b> , lapsus sum,
		3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. dep.
				n.</i> and <i>a.</i>, <i>to
			fall</i>, <i>slip</i>, <i>slide</i>,
				<i>glide</i>, or <i>flow between</i>
				(<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per has stellis interlabentibus umbras,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 2, 649</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(in tmesi), inter enim labentur aquae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 2, 349</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sil. 6, 18</span></i>.—With <i>acc.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fluvius lucos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 22, 8, 17</span></i>
			.</div>
